[Pass 4, iter 2 re-review — structured output requested]

Previously RESOLVED in this pass: everything except the seven PARTIALs. Do not re-litigate those.

The seven PARTIALs you reported (A2 launchURL scheme gate, A12 Linux anonymous jar, A30 block-server matching, A31 handler.next, A37 refresh coalescing, B16 FLV chunk performance, B17 missing mp4-join test) were worked on. Notes from the fixers, for your judgement:

- A2: http/https open directly; file/content/javascript/data/blob/about/filesystem stay hard-blocked; every OTHER scheme now goes through a confirmation dialog naming scheme + target before reaching the OS (a deliberate design choice, not an oversight — custom app schemes are legitimate on these pages).
- A12: `onLogoutMain` now calls `clearWebCookies()` then `setAnonymousWebCookie()` on all platforms; the Linux early-return in `setAnonymousWebCookie` is documented as a correct no-op because desktop_webview_window exposes no set-cookie API and `WebviewPage.openLinux` injects the anonymous buvid3 at documentStart for every window.
- A30: new `parseBlockServer` requires http(s) + host, rejects userinfo and the bilibili domain family; `_isBlockServer` matches scheme+host+port+path-prefix and returns false when the saved value is rejected.
- A31: the retry path ends in `handler.next(error)`, with a `finish()` helper so a failure is delivered once rather than once per retry level (the fixer measured 3 deliveries with retryCount=2 before adding it).
- A37: refresh coalescing.
- B16: the fixer first argued grouping was impossible, then measured: a synthetic 10-minute FLV (41,087 samples) took 49,570 ms to remux; after buffered I/O plus ~1 s chunk grouping it takes 185 ms, chunks 41,087 -> 1,193, stco 164,380 -> 4,804 B, moov -45%. Both changes are in the shared writer, so the DASH path benefits too. Judge the correctness of the buffering/window and grouping logic, not the intent.
- B17: a join test was added to test/utils/flv_demux_test.dart.

Incremental diff (this refinement only):

